framework DecisionAudit
problem P1:
  "Continue from the confirmed MCP incident release judgment into a concrete local release-boundary candidate"
step S1:
  evidence E1:
    "Current branch is codex/issue-21-plan-review at e39c739f plus retained uncommitted changes; package version is still 0.11.1. Accepted Plan Review specification defines Grammar 10 and CLI Contract 11. Technical acceptance and all 1421 unit tests passed"
  evidence E2:
    "Accepted ADR 0003 uses suffix-free beta minor releases for new grammar and CLI contract boundaries, and prior release procedures separate version selection, source preparation, immutable candidate acceptance and publication"
  premise PR1:
    "The owner confirmed that original MCP causal attribution is not a blocker after a successful rerun and instructed proceeding. Timeout adjustment is separate work"
  pending U1:
    "The owner has not yet selected the next release version or authorized publication; fresh remote and registry state have not been checked in this local review"
step S2:
  pending A1:
    "Propose suffix-free 0.12.0 as the next beta minor for Grammar 10 and CLI Contract 11, retaining exact 0.11.1 as the previous public rollback pin"
  pending A2:
    "A 0.11.x patch would understate the new grammar, result identities and CLI contract boundary; defer version mutation until the owner selects the exact target"
step S3:
  decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, PR1, U1, A1, A2:
    "Produce a local candidate review of the 0.12.0 beta boundary and the remaining release steps. Preserve dirty source and canonical completed feature plan. Do not change package versions, create a new governed plan, commit, publish or assert acceptance receipts. Present the concrete candidate for the required version decision"
